Sorry that was page 353 in the Intro.  But pick up any intro stats book
and you should find it for the case of unpaired samples with different
variances.  For example for a t-test it is on page 115 of Snedecor and
Cochran, Statistical Methods 6th edition but you'll need to find an old
guy like me to find that particular text.  I purchased it in 1973 at the
outrageous price of $8.20.

--jeff

